notes.body:
The point is the functions added for supporting the deinterlacing strategy are not (yet) covering all possible conversations cases. To address this, either a full copy/paste of the historical existing code then following the very same logic, or going step by step as I initially started. The first method would probably work but if there is unreachable code at some places it won't be discovered (it can be the case, or not). The second one triggers such unexpected results but help me to track all cases.

For now, to solve this particular RTP behavior, it could be :

```
-        conv=conversation_new_strat(pinfo, CONVERSATION_UDP, 0);

         /* For new conversations, check if there is a NO_PORT_B conv matching
          * on the reverse direction and in this case set the appropriate dissector
@@ -1232,11 +1231,18 @@ dissect(tvbuff_t *tvb, packet_info *pinfo, proto_tree *tree, uint32_t ip_proto)

         if(revconvnob) {
             // apply the higher protocol dissector
+            conv=conversation_new_strat(pinfo, CONVERSATION_UDP, 0);
             dissector_handle_t l7_handle = conversation_get_dissector(revconvnob, pinfo->num);
             if(l7_handle) {
                 conversation_set_dissector(conv, l7_handle);
             }
         }
+        else {
+            revconvnob = find_conversation_strat(pinfo, CONVERSATION_UDP, 0, false);
+        }
```

